    "narrative": "The Austin Waves look to capitalize on several high-upside matchups today, led by **Gunnar Henderson**, who earns our highest daily efficiency score of 83.29. Facing off against Brown, this is a prime spot for **Gunnar Henderson** to anchor the offense, bolstered by a significant +14% dynamic platoon advantage and a favorable batting order position. Close behind is **Kyle Tucker** (79.07), who faces a soft target in Yarbrough; despite a minor platoon drag, his elite profile makes him a must-start. **Andy Pages** (73.31) also projects well, utilizing a substantial +18% SP skill edge to capitalize on the same favorable matchup against Yarbrough. These three represent the core of our output today, balancing high-ceiling potential with advantageous matchups against mid-tier starting pitching.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision today was benching **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (56.83). Despite his status as a perennial threat, **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** fell just short of the efficiency threshold required to displace players like **Josh Jung** or **Miguel Vargas**, who both benefited from more favorable opponent SP_xERA ratings. While **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** remains a high-floor option, the optimizer favored the structural lineup advantages provided to the starting core. We are also keeping a close eye on **Drake Baldwin**, whose score of 49.27 sits near the marginal line due to a tough draw against Eovaldi, though his spot atop the lineup provides enough cushion to remain in the starting nine. With no significant weather threats reported, the primary risk remains the inherent volatility of the matchups against Eovaldi and Gilbert, L; however, the overall alignment suggests a productive day on the basepaths and at the plate.",
